 "verified-authoritative/subproblem-lookup/bypass-after-flight-install"
 :minimized-fixture "fixture.edn"
 :impact :other
 :affected-versions
 ["PR 101 worktree before authoritative lookup transition routing"]
 :affected-backends [:shared :datomic :datascript :datahike]
 :root-cause
 "The host selected or installed a cache flight before invoking the generated lookup decision. The returned generated action only controlled a later recursive-bypass branch, so verified-authoritative lookup was not authoritative over the state transition it purported to decide. A divergent bypass action could leave an unrealized registered flight and incomplete entry behind."
 :fix
 "The generated lookup action is now selected from the lifecycle-stable candidate state inside the store transition and is dispatched before any flight installation. Resolve and lookup consume that selected action for complete-hit versus join/start behavior instead of recomputing or ignoring it. The strict boundary rejects any generated action that contradicts its validated candidate state."
 :closing-evidence
 ["eacl.subproblem-cache-test/authoritative-lookup-action-precedes-storage-mutation-test"
  "formal mutation :lookup-decision-after-flight-installation"
  "formal/dafny/SubproblemCache.dfy recursive bypass flight-installation lemma"]}
